%% Figure: Asynchronous payment, ticket issuance and email (CU-06, CU-07).
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor C as Customer
    participant O as Order service API
    participant PQ as SQS payment-requests
    participant W as Payment worker (in order task)
    participant DB as MySQL
    participant Q as Queue service
    participant OE as SQS order-events
    participant T as Ticket service consumer
    participant N as Notification service
    participant M as Gmail SMTP

    C->>O: POST /orders/77/payment-requests {paymentToken "simulated"}
    O->>O: verify JWT, order owner, status PENDING or PAID
    O->>PQ: PaymentRequested v1 {orderId, customerSub}, delay 7 s
    O-->>C: 202 PROCESSING
    loop every 2 s, up to 30 polls
        C->>O: GET /orders/77
    end
    PQ->>W: long poll (20 s), visibility 60 s
    W->>DB: BEGIN, SELECT order FOR UPDATE
    alt order already PAID (duplicate delivery)
        W->>DB: COMMIT, re-publish OrderPaid only (no second capture)
    else hold ACTIVE and not expired
        W->>DB: SELECT hold FOR UPDATE
        W->>DB: seats HELD to SOLD (row count must equal quantity)<br/>or reserved_qty to sold_qty for Tier 1
        W->>DB: hold CONFIRMED, INSERT payment CAPTURED, order PAID
        W->>DB: queue entry LEFT, COMMIT
        W->>Q: POST /events/42/queue/admit-next (x-internal-token, 1 s timeout)
        W->>OE: OrderPaid v1, delay 10 s
    else hold expired
        W->>DB: release hold, order FAILED, COMMIT
    end
    W->>PQ: delete message
    Note over PQ: After 5 failed receives the message moves to the DLQ<br/>and the CloudWatch alarm fires
    OE->>T: long poll, up to 10 messages
    T->>DB: GET_LOCK("ticket-order-77"), BEGIN
    T->>DB: SELECT existing tickets FOR UPDATE, INSERT missing ones (random qr_token)
    T->>DB: COMMIT, RELEASE_LOCK
    T->>OE: delete message
    T-)N: POST /notifications/order-confirmation (fire and forget)
    loop each ticket
        N->>DB: skip if this ticket already SENT
        N->>M: send email with this ticket's QR code
        N->>DB: record SENT or FAILED (unique on ticket_id)
    end
    C->>T: GET /customers/me/tickets (polled every 5 s)
    Note over T,DB: Reconciliation sweep in the ticket service issues tickets<br/>for any PAID order the consumer missed
